# Implementation of a Consistent Dynamic Game World in a Text Adventure Based on Large Language Models

## My interpretation of the brief

The project is a text adventure game where an LLM generates the story and interactions while the program maintains a consistent game world and game state. The player can interact with the world using natural language, and the system should ensure that important information such as characters, locations, items, and previous events remains consistent throughout the game.

## Why I am a good fit for this project

I am interested in AI, games, and interactive applications. I would like to learn how LLMs can be used to create interactive game experiences. I also think this project is a good opportunity for me to improve my programming skills while working on a practical AI-based application.

## Relevant experience and background

I have basic programming knowledge from my Computer Science Engineering studies. I am familiar with fundamental programming concepts and GitHub, and I am motivated to learn the technologies required for this project. I am also interested in learning more about LLMs and how they can be integrated into applications.

## Proposed approach

I would first build a simple text adventure with a basic game state and predefined game rules. Then I would integrate an LLM to generate dynamic story content and responses to player actions. The program would store important world information separately from the generated text so that the game world remains consistent. I would start with a small and manageable game world and gradually add more features.

## Initial plan

1. Define the game world, entities, and basic game rules.
2. Build a simple text adventure and game-state management system.
3. Integrate an LLM for dynamic story generation.
4. Add mechanisms for maintaining consistency of characters, locations, items, and events.
5. Test the system with different player interactions and improve the consistency of the generated world.
